    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d648">

                <pb facs="0940" n="812" xml:id="pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">820.7961 Dept. of Commerce Flight/9:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Poindexter</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-17T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Your cable number 1, January 7, 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">8</hi>] p.m.<anchor
                        n="89" xml:id="d648-f1"/> Peruvian Government authorizes with great pleasure
                    flight over Peruvian soil, free entry of planes, equipment and supplies, and
                    will give full and complete friendly reception to the expedition, aiding in
                    every way possible the success of the purposes which it has in view.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Poindexter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d648-f1" n="89" xml:id="d648-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 2 to the Ambassador in Brazil, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi></p>
